1
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Zankoku na tenshi no you ni

2
00:00:00,990 --> 00:00:06,930
Just like the cruel angel

3
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

4
00:00:06,930 --> 00:00:14,590
Young boy, become a legend

5
00:00:18,990 --> 00:00:22,410
2D4U PRESENTS:

6
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Aoi kaze ga ima

7
00:00:22,770 --> 00:00:25,810
Even though the untested breeze...

8
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
mune no doa o tataitemo

9
00:00:25,810 --> 00:00:29,510
...taps at the door to your heart

10
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
Watashi dake o tada mitsumete hohoenderu anata

11
00:00:29,510 --> 00:00:36,970
You just look solely at me and smile

12
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
Sotto fureru mono motomeru koto ni muchuu de

13
00:00:37,560 --> 00:00:44,500
So intent on seeking out that gentle touch

14
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Unmei sae mada shiranai itaike na hitomi

15
00:00:44,500 --> 00:00:51,400
Such innocent eyes, still ignorant of their destiny

16
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
Dakedo itsuka kizuku deshou

17
00:00:52,000 --> 00:00:55,750
But someday, you are sure to realize...

18
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
sono senaka ni wa

19
00:00:55,750 --> 00:00:58,340
...that upon your back

20
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
Haruka mirai mezasu tame

21
00:00:59,510 --> 00:01:02,960
You have the wings with which to fly...

22
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
no hane ga aru koto

23
00:01:02,960 --> 00:01:06,310
...towards the distant future

24
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
Zankoku na tenshi no teeze

25
00:01:06,990 --> 00:01:10,690
The cruel angel's thesis

26
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Madobe kara yagate tobidatsu

27
00:01:10,690 --> 00:01:14,430
Soon, you will take flight from the windowsill

28
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
Hotobashiru atsui patosu de

29
00:01:14,430 --> 00:01:18,200
With your torrent of ardent pathos

30
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
Omoide o uragiru nara

31
00:01:18,200 --> 00:01:21,900
If you are to betray our memories

32
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
Kono sora o daite kagayaku

33
00:01:21,900 --> 00:01:25,540
You, who embrace these heavens and shine

34
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Shounen yo shinwa ni nare

35
00:01:25,540 --> 00:01:29,270
Young boy, become a legend

36
00:01:33,360 --> 00:01:35,570
Are you ready, Shinji?

37
00:01:35,570 --> 00:01:36,650
Yes.

38
00:01:36,650 --> 00:01:38,660
Release the final safety lock!

39
00:01:39,740 --> 00:01:42,620
Evangelion Unit 01, lift off!

40
00:01:45,330 --> 00:01:49,250
Shinji, just concentrate on walking right now.

41
00:01:49,630 --> 00:01:50,920
Walk...

42
00:02:00,090 --> 00:02:01,140
It walked!

43
00:02:04,020 --> 00:02:05,220
Walk...

44
00:02:14,030 --> 00:02:16,690
Shinji, get it together!

45
00:02:16,690 --> 00:02:18,820
Hurry! Get up!

46
00:02:29,830 --> 00:02:33,040
Shinji, calm down! That's not your arm!

47
00:02:36,710 --> 00:02:38,420
What's going on with the
Eva's defense system?

48
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,050
The signal's not working!

49
00:02:40,050 --> 00:02:41,800
The field's not deploying!

50
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,720
Have we failed?

51
00:02:47,850 --> 00:02:48,980
Left arm damaged!

52
00:02:48,980 --> 00:02:49,980
The circuits have disconnected!

53
00:02:52,480 --> 00:02:54,320
Shinji, dodge!

54
00:03:00,150 --> 00:03:01,860
There's a crack on the front of the cranium!

55
00:03:01,860 --> 00:03:03,530
The armor won't last much longer!

56
00:03:12,790 --> 00:03:14,630
The head's been damaged!
Extent of damage, unknown!

57
00:03:14,630 --> 00:03:17,260
The control nerves are disconnecting
one after another!

58
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:19,010
We're not getting any readings on the pilot!

59
00:03:20,010 --> 00:03:20,930
Shinji!

60
00:03:52,830 --> 00:03:54,420
I don't know this ceiling.

61
00:03:54,460 --> 00:03:57,920
EPISODE 02
UNFAMILIAR
CEILING

62
00:04:09,890 --> 00:04:11,770
So, the Angels have returned, eh?

63
00:04:11,770 --> 00:04:13,520
It's so sudden.

64
00:04:13,520 --> 00:04:15,560
It's the same as it was fifteen years ago.

65
00:04:15,560 --> 00:04:19,610
A disaster comes as it will, without warning.

66
00:04:19,610 --> 00:04:25,990
We could say it was fortunate, in the sense
that our prior investments were not a waste.

67
00:04:25,990 --> 00:04:28,410
You can't be sure about that yet.

68
00:04:28,410 --> 00:04:30,790
If it doesn't pay off, it's a waste all the same.

69
00:04:30,790 --> 00:04:32,580
Precisely. Now that the Angels,

70
00:04:32,580 --> 00:04:35,750
and the fact that we have been
manipulating information,

71
00:04:35,750 --> 00:04:37,710
have become public knowledge,

72
00:04:37,710 --> 00:04:44,090
Nerv must operate in a speedy
and prudent manner.

73
00:04:44,090 --> 00:04:48,220
It's already been taken care of.
You may rest assured of that.

74
00:04:48,430 --> 00:04:52,520
<i>In regards to the declaration of
the special state of emergency,</i>

75
00:04:52,520 --> 00:04:54,100
<i>government officials have announced...</i>

76
00:04:54,100 --> 00:04:55,310
<i>This incident was...</i>

77
00:04:55,310 --> 00:04:56,520
<i>UN forces in Japan...</i>

78
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:59,440
So it's public scenario B-22.

79
00:04:56,520 --> 00:04:59,860
<i>In response to reporters' questions...</i>

80
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:03,110
<i>No, there's no threat of contamination
from the center of the explosion.</i>

81
00:04:59,860 --> 00:05:02,440
So, we're hushing up the truth again?

82
00:05:02,440 --> 00:05:04,320
But at least our PR people are thrilled

83
00:05:03,110 --> 00:05:06,860
<i>The only Angel samples collected
were adhered to the Eva.</i>

84
00:05:04,320 --> 00:05:06,360
Now that they've finally got something to do.

85
00:05:06,360 --> 00:05:08,620
We're being pretty casual about it.

86
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:12,870
<i>Correct, as in the model simulation,
approximately 99.9% of it evaporated.</i>

87
00:05:08,620 --> 00:05:12,040
I don't know about that.
I think everyone's actually scared.

88
00:05:12,870 --> 00:05:13,910
Of course we are.

89
00:05:14,790 --> 00:05:17,250
Well, we must acknowledge that.

90
00:05:17,250 --> 00:05:19,290
Speaking of which, Ikari,

91
00:05:19,290 --> 00:05:22,840
isn't there a better way to
utilize Nerv and Eva?

92
00:05:22,840 --> 00:05:24,630
First the repairs to Unit 00,

93
00:05:24,630 --> 00:05:28,220
and now to Unit 01, which you
wrecked in its first battle.

94
00:05:28,220 --> 00:05:30,260
It's enough to bankrupt an entire country.

95
00:05:30,260 --> 00:05:34,810
We also understand that you
gave that toy to your son.

96
00:05:34,810 --> 00:05:38,310
Manpower, time, and money.

97
00:05:38,310 --> 00:05:41,480
How much more do you and your family
plan on wasting?

98
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:44,400
<i>And that is not your only responsibility.</i>

99
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:46,030
Top Secret

100
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:46,030
Human Instrumentality Project

101
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:46,030
United Nations Top Executive Meeting

102
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:46,030
17th Midterm Report

103
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:46,030
Human Instrumentality Committee

104
00:05:44,110 --> 00:05:46,030
2015 Business Plan Outline Summary

105
00:05:44,400 --> 00:05:46,030
<i>The Human Instrumentality Project,</i>

106
00:05:46,360 --> 00:05:48,820
that should be your top priority.

107
00:05:48,820 --> 00:05:49,870
Precisely.

108
00:05:49,870 --> 00:05:57,120
Under these desperate circumstances,
that project is our one and only hope.

109
00:05:57,120 --> 00:06:00,500
In any case, we cannot excuse any delays
in that project's schedule

110
00:06:00,500 --> 00:06:02,590
due to the reappearance of the Angels.

111
00:06:02,920 --> 00:06:05,920
We will consider the issue
regarding the budget.

112
00:06:05,920 --> 00:06:08,800
Now, the rest of this meeting
concerns only the committee.

113
00:06:08,800 --> 00:06:11,260
Your presence here was appreciated, Ikari.

114
00:06:13,430 --> 00:06:17,230
Ikari, there is no turning back.

115
00:06:19,520 --> 00:06:21,440
I know.

116
00:06:21,980 --> 00:06:24,320
Mankind has no time left.

117
00:06:51,390 --> 00:06:54,060
Air conditioning has just got to be
mankind's greatest treasure.

118
00:06:54,060 --> 00:06:56,560
It's the triumph of science over nature.

119
00:06:56,560 --> 00:06:58,140
Shinji's woken up.

120
00:06:58,890 --> 00:07:00,940
How is he?

121
00:07:00,940 --> 00:07:04,480
No external injuries. His memory
is a bit muddled, however.

122
00:07:04,900 --> 00:07:07,320
You don't think it could it be
mental contamination?

123
00:07:07,320 --> 00:07:09,570
There appears to be no cause for worry.

124
00:07:09,570 --> 00:07:10,860
Really?

125
00:07:11,860 --> 00:07:15,200
I suppose he did have a pretty hectic day.

126
00:07:15,200 --> 00:07:19,330
It's not suprising. His cranial nerves
took a lot of strain.

127
00:07:19,330 --> 00:07:21,960
Don't you mean his heart?

128
00:07:37,810 --> 00:07:40,520
Construction Plan Notice

129
00:07:42,520 --> 00:07:45,980
Okay, okay. Keep it coming. Good!

130
00:07:49,690 --> 00:07:52,660
If Eva and this city both operate
at their full potential,

131
00:07:52,660 --> 00:07:54,240
maybe we can make it through this.

132
00:07:54,240 --> 00:07:57,870
Are you going to defeat the Angels?
You're always such an optimist.

133
00:07:57,870 --> 00:08:02,210
Hey, sometimes you need a little wishful
thinking just to keep on living.

134
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:07,420
I see your point. It helps to
hear things like that from you.

135
00:08:08,250 --> 00:08:08,920
See ya!

136
00:08:47,880 --> 00:08:49,800
Are you sure?

137
00:08:49,800 --> 00:08:51,510
They don't want to live together?

138
00:08:51,510 --> 00:08:56,720
I think that living apart is natural
for Ikari and his son.

139
00:08:56,720 --> 00:09:00,310
And being together is unnatural?

140
00:09:00,310 --> 00:09:02,220
Shinji Ikari

141
00:09:00,770 --> 00:09:02,220
Alone?

142
00:09:02,220 --> 00:09:06,230
Right. His room will be in the 6th Block,
just beyond this one.

143
00:09:06,230 --> 00:09:07,650
Is that satisfactory?

144
00:09:07,650 --> 00:09:08,900
Yes.

145
00:09:09,610 --> 00:09:11,280
Are you sure?

146
00:09:11,280 --> 00:09:12,530
Shinji...

147
00:09:12,530 --> 00:09:14,400
It's fine. I'd rather be alone.

148
00:09:15,490 --> 00:09:17,820
Anywhere is fine.

149
00:09:17,820 --> 00:09:19,080
What?!

150
00:09:19,080 --> 00:09:23,830
So, I said, I'll take care of Shinji.

151
00:09:23,830 --> 00:09:25,710
I've already got permission from the brass.

152
00:09:26,080 --> 00:09:29,040
Hey, it's not like I'm going to
"put the moves" on a kid.

153
00:09:29,040 --> 00:09:30,170
<i>Of course you're not!</i>

154
00:09:30,170 --> 00:09:32,460
<i>What the hell are you thinking?</i>

155
00:09:32,460 --> 00:09:32,760
<i>You're always like that. Honestly!</i>

156
00:09:32,760 --> 00:09:35,340
<i>You're always like that. Honestly!</i>
She just can't take a joke.

157
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:42,640
Well, we'll have to have a party tonight, right?

158
00:09:43,560 --> 00:09:44,810
What for?

159
00:09:44,810 --> 00:09:48,270
A welcoming party for my
new roommate, of course!

160
00:09:52,690 --> 00:09:54,900
So, you're going to move after all?

161
00:09:55,240 --> 00:10:00,660
Yes. I never dreamed that this city
would become a battlefield.

162
00:10:00,660 --> 00:10:02,450
Yeah.

163
00:10:02,450 --> 00:10:06,460
My husband's saying that our kid and I
should evacuate, at the very least.

164
00:10:06,460 --> 00:10:08,210
Evacuate, huh?

165
00:10:08,210 --> 00:10:12,170
This city may be a fortress, but that's
no guarantee of safety.

166
00:10:12,170 --> 00:10:15,590
Just remembering yesterday
gives me the chills.

167
00:10:20,760 --> 00:10:24,810
I hope you don't mind if we make
a little stop on the way.

168
00:10:24,810 --> 00:10:25,890
Where?

169
00:10:26,640 --> 00:10:28,230
Someplace really cool.

170
00:10:34,190 --> 00:10:38,030
It's just such a lonely city.

171
00:10:39,990 --> 00:10:40,870
It's time.

172
00:11:06,850 --> 00:11:10,100
Amazing! The buildings are growing!

173
00:11:25,080 --> 00:11:28,620
This city is a fortress, designed to
protect against the Angels.

174
00:11:29,210 --> 00:11:31,250
This is New Tokyo-3.

175
00:11:31,580 --> 00:11:33,000
This is our city.

176
00:11:35,130 --> 00:11:39,340
And it's the city that you helped to protect.

177
00:11:52,520 --> 00:11:55,400
Your things should have already
been delivered, Shinji.

178
00:11:55,860 --> 00:12:00,240
The truth is, I just recently moved
to this city too.

179
00:12:00,740 --> 00:12:02,450
Come on in.

180
00:12:02,450 --> 00:12:06,160
Pardon the intrusion.

181
00:12:07,080 --> 00:12:10,330
Shinji, this is YOUR home now.

182
00:12:16,960 --> 00:12:19,170
I'm home.

183
00:12:19,550 --> 00:12:21,260
Welcome home.

184
00:12:22,800 --> 00:12:26,140
As you can see, the place
is a little bit messy,

185
00:12:26,140 --> 00:12:27,680
but make yourself comfortable.

186
00:12:29,430 --> 00:12:30,980
You call this

187
00:12:32,060 --> 00:12:33,600
a "little bit" messy?

188
00:12:33,810 --> 00:12:37,360
Oh! Sorry! Could you put the food
in the fridge?

189
00:12:37,360 --> 00:12:38,820
Sure.

190
00:12:39,860 --> 00:12:41,360
Ice,

191
00:12:41,360 --> 00:12:42,780
snacks,

192
00:12:43,280 --> 00:12:45,200
and nothing but beer.

193
00:12:45,530 --> 00:12:47,830
What kind of a life does she lead?

194
00:12:55,670 --> 00:12:57,920
Excuse me. What's in the other fridge?

195
00:12:57,920 --> 00:13:01,960
Oh, don't mind that.
He's probably still sleeping!

196
00:13:01,960 --> 00:13:03,170
Sleeping?

197
00:13:05,180 --> 00:13:07,430
Let's eat!

198
00:13:07,430 --> 00:13:08,430
Let's eat.

199
00:13:16,980 --> 00:13:21,860
Life just doesn't get any better than this!

200
00:13:22,690 --> 00:13:26,660
Don't you want to eat?
It's pretty good, even if it is instant.

201
00:13:27,280 --> 00:13:31,330
I'm sorry, I'm just not used to it.

202
00:13:31,330 --> 00:13:34,160
That's no excuse! You can't be so finicky.

203
00:13:34,870 --> 00:13:38,790
No, that's not what I... well...

204
00:13:39,340 --> 00:13:40,460
Isn't this nice?

205
00:13:41,630 --> 00:13:44,050
Having dinner with somebody else!

206
00:13:44,050 --> 00:13:46,680
Uh, yes.

207
00:13:48,970 --> 00:13:51,760
Here we go for the next one.

208
00:13:51,760 --> 00:13:53,810
Rock, paper, scissors...

209
00:13:54,350 --> 00:13:58,190
Pon! Pon! Pon! Pon!

210
00:13:59,440 --> 00:14:01,230
Sorry, Shinji.

211
00:14:01,230 --> 00:14:06,360
Our Chores Chart

212
00:14:01,230 --> 00:14:06,360
Day/Chore     Su      M      T     W      Th        F       S

213
00:14:01,230 --> 00:14:06,360
Breakfast     S        S       M       S      S        S       S

214
00:14:01,230 --> 00:14:06,360
Dinner         S        S       S      M      S        S       M

215
00:14:01,230 --> 00:14:06,360
Okay! That should be it for fairly
splitting up the chores!

216
00:14:06,860 --> 00:14:07,950
Yes.

217
00:14:07,950 --> 00:14:11,240
Starting today, this is your home,

218
00:14:11,450 --> 00:14:13,580
so you can take advantage
of everything here.

219
00:14:14,240 --> 00:14:15,580
Yes.

220
00:14:15,580 --> 00:14:19,420
Man. All you keep saying is yes, yes, yes.
It's so depressing!

221
00:14:19,420 --> 00:14:23,420
You're a boy, aren't you?
Act like a man! Okay?

222
00:14:23,420 --> 00:14:25,050
Yes.

223
00:14:25,050 --> 00:14:26,260
Oh well.

224
00:14:26,590 --> 00:14:31,470
Why don't you go take a bath and
scrub away all those bad memories?

225
00:14:31,470 --> 00:14:33,430
Bathing is the laundry of life.

226
00:14:42,400 --> 00:14:44,940
Miss Misato!

227
00:14:44,940 --> 00:14:45,860
What?

228
00:14:45,860 --> 00:14:48,360
A p... p... p...

229
00:14:48,740 --> 00:14:49,950
What?

230
00:14:50,530 --> 00:14:54,160
Oh, him? He's one of those new
hot spring penguins.

231
00:15:02,920 --> 00:15:04,670
What...

232
00:15:04,670 --> 00:15:08,090
His name is Pen Pen.
He's your other roommate.

233
00:15:08,880 --> 00:15:11,260
Why don't you cover that up?

234
00:15:09,050 --> 00:15:17,430
Toothpicks

235
00:15:17,770 --> 00:15:20,480
I wonder if I've been a little bit TOO cheery?

236
00:15:21,230 --> 00:15:23,360
Maybe I'm the one who's transparent.

237
00:15:24,610 --> 00:15:26,780
Miss Misato Katsuragi.

238
00:15:28,530 --> 00:15:30,200
She's not a bad person.

239
00:15:30,700 --> 00:15:32,450
Bathing is the laundry of life.

240
00:15:33,120 --> 00:15:37,330
But bad memories always seem to find me
when I'm in the bath.

241
00:15:38,450 --> 00:15:39,750
My father

242
00:15:40,870 --> 00:15:42,210
and Rei Ayanami...

243
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:48,050
So, how was Rei today?

244
00:15:49,800 --> 00:15:53,010
You went to the hospital this
afternoon, didn't you?

245
00:15:54,010 --> 00:15:56,310
She'll be ready to work again in twenty days.

246
00:15:56,310 --> 00:16:00,310
By then, we'll be ready to re-activate
Unit 00 from cryo-stasis.

247
00:16:00,850 --> 00:16:03,560
It must be so hard on those children.

248
00:16:04,100 --> 00:16:07,150
There is no one else who can pilot the Evas.

249
00:16:07,150 --> 00:16:09,940
As long as they survive, that is what
I'll have them do.

250
00:16:09,940 --> 00:16:13,610
With no regard to what they may want?

251
00:16:13,950 --> 00:16:15,870
Little Shin's Room

252
00:16:22,410 --> 00:16:24,170
No. 1 Public Middle School Transfer Application
Shinji Ikari

253
00:16:31,380 --> 00:16:34,470
Yeah, after all the horrible stuff
he went through,

254
00:16:34,470 --> 00:16:36,680
there's no telling if he'll pilot it again.

255
00:16:37,220 --> 00:16:40,220
Maintaining him is part of your job.

256
00:16:40,890 --> 00:16:43,980
I'm just scared. I don't know
how to deal with him.

257
00:16:43,980 --> 00:16:47,980
Grumbling already? You were the one
who had the bright idea of taking him in.

258
00:16:47,980 --> 00:16:48,860
Shut up!

259
00:16:50,400 --> 00:16:54,910
That time, I was thinking of Shinji as a tool.

260
00:16:55,410 --> 00:16:57,120
I'm as bad as Ritsuko.

261
00:16:57,780 --> 00:17:00,040
We destroyed that Angel.

262
00:17:01,790 --> 00:17:03,250
But I guess I can't be happy about it.

263
00:17:05,790 --> 00:17:08,420
Another ceiling I don't know.

264
00:17:10,420 --> 00:17:15,380
Of course. In this whole city,
there's no place that's familiar.

265
00:17:16,260 --> 00:17:18,260
This is your home.

266
00:17:20,890 --> 00:17:22,720
Why am I here?

267
00:17:44,750 --> 00:17:46,920
The head has been damaged!
Extent of damage, unknown!

268
00:17:46,920 --> 00:17:48,750
We're having problems
maintaining activation!

269
00:17:48,750 --> 00:17:49,710
Status report!

270
00:17:49,710 --> 00:17:52,590
The synchrograph is reversing!
The pulses are flowing backward!

271
00:17:52,590 --> 00:17:54,260
Break the circuit! Block it!

272
00:17:54,260 --> 00:17:55,090
We can't!

273
00:17:55,090 --> 00:17:57,220
It's rejecting the signal! It won't take it!

274
00:17:57,220 --> 00:17:58,470
What about Shinji?

275
00:17:58,470 --> 00:18:00,600
His monitors aren't responding.
Life signs unknown!

276
00:18:00,600 --> 00:18:02,510
Unit 01 's gone completely silent!

277
00:18:02,510 --> 00:18:03,560
Misato!

278
00:18:03,930 --> 00:18:05,390
This is it.

279
00:18:05,390 --> 00:18:08,060
Abort the operation!
Rescuing the pilot is our first priority!

280
00:18:08,060 --> 00:18:09,690
Force eject the entry plug!

281
00:18:09,690 --> 00:18:12,070
We can't! It's completely out of control!

282
00:18:12,070 --> 00:18:13,070
What the hell?!

283
00:18:21,490 --> 00:18:22,950
The Eva's re-activating!

284
00:18:22,950 --> 00:18:24,950
Impossible! There's no way it can move!

285
00:18:26,120 --> 00:18:27,410
It can't be...

286
00:18:27,410 --> 00:18:28,210
It's gone berserk?

287
00:18:49,020 --> 00:18:50,020
It looks like we've won.

288
00:18:56,110 --> 00:18:57,190
An AT field!

289
00:18:57,780 --> 00:19:00,450
No! As long as the Angel
has that AT field up...

290
00:19:00,450 --> 00:19:01,780
He can't touch the Angel!

291
00:19:05,200 --> 00:19:06,620
Left arm, regenerated!

292
00:19:06,620 --> 00:19:07,290
Incredible!

293
00:19:11,330 --> 00:19:13,380
Unit 01 has deployed its AT field!

294
00:19:13,960 --> 00:19:16,050
It's neutralizing the phase space!

295
00:19:16,510 --> 00:19:18,630
No, it's eroding it!

296
00:19:22,680 --> 00:19:25,220
It went through that AT field so easily...

297
00:20:09,390 --> 00:20:10,310
It's going to self-destruct?!

298
00:20:23,030 --> 00:20:23,820
Is the Eva...

299
00:20:34,000 --> 00:20:35,790
That must be the Eva's...

300
00:20:35,790 --> 00:20:37,290
true form.

301
00:20:44,430 --> 00:20:45,890
Circuits reconnected.

302
00:20:45,890 --> 00:20:48,310
Systems restored. Graphs back to normal.

303
00:20:48,310 --> 00:20:50,140
Pilot life signs, confirmed.

304
00:20:50,140 --> 00:20:52,060
Send out the recovery team. Hurry!

305
00:20:52,060 --> 00:20:54,020
Preserving the pilot's life is our first priority.

306
00:21:36,980 --> 00:21:39,520
Shinji, I'm coming in.

307
00:21:42,610 --> 00:21:44,820
I forgot to tell you something.

308
00:21:45,700 --> 00:21:48,910
You did a very praiseworthy thing today.

309
00:21:49,200 --> 00:21:50,660
You should be proud of yourself.

310
00:21:51,700 --> 00:21:53,500
Good night, Shinji.

311
00:21:55,870 --> 00:21:57,120
Hang in there.

312
00:21:57,170 --> 00:22:00,460
To Be Continued

313
00:23:05,900 --> 00:23:06,860
Preview

314
00:23:06,400 --> 00:23:09,780
As Shinji lives his new life,
drifting along without direction,

315
00:23:09,780 --> 00:23:11,780
there was no way for him to make friends.

316
00:23:11,780 --> 00:23:15,870
But the fact that he is an Eva pilot
makes him popular in his class.

317
00:23:15,870 --> 00:23:17,660
Next Evangelion: "The Silent Phone"

318
00:23:17,660 --> 00:23:19,790
I'll give you fan service next time too!

319
00:23:18,830 --> 00:23:20,920
THE SILENT PHONE
